>> title: Cachete
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, cheek, mexican, oven, braise, tacos
>> counters: Taquería, One Pot
>> aka: cachete, cabeza, taco de cabeza, tacos de cachete, beef cheek, barbacoa de cachete, cachetes de res
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, salsa-verde
>> servings: 6
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: forgiving — the silverskin comes off before the pot goes on, because nothing in the oven will render it and it stays as gristle
>> washing-up: the Dutch oven

Preheat the #oven{} to 300°F (150°C).

>> step: season in the pot
Season @beef cheeks{3%lb}(1.4 kg; trimmed of the tough silverskin) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs} and @coarse black pepper{1%tsp} in a #Dutch oven{}.

>> step: add the pot vegetables
Add @white onion{1}(quartered), @garlic{6%cloves}, @bay leaves{2}, @dried Mexican oregano{1%tsp}, @whole cloves{3}, @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, @avocado leaves{2}(optional, toasted), and @water{2%cup}(475 mL) to @&(~1)seasoned cheeks{}, which should sit half submerged rather than swimming.

>> step: braise 300°F 3 hr
Braise @&(~1)pot{} covered at 300°F for ~braise{3%hr}, until a cheek gives way to the back of a spoon with no pull left in it.

>> step: shred coarse, salt
Shred @&(~1)braised cheeks{} coarsely with two forks, moistening them with their own liquor, and salt with @kosher salt{1%tsp}.
